-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gunfright
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Gunfright (1985)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         0cd9e86a2c6c7afa22025f8d593af093

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (-1.08% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe A3C6
              (the player's own update); 3 trials per scene with different R
              seeds; figures are the fastest trial; every trial faster than
              the original by 0.3 to 1.2%, none slower; player state equal to
              the original at every update)

  Changes     1.0: the town and duels on the Next's hardware sprite layer at
              the original's pace; the original loading screen; Sinclair's 48K
              ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed
              restored after every hook; eight cheats from the archive, ammo
              and money corrected.

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 3 starts; on the keyboard X and C move
              left and right, A up, 1 down and Q fires. The original game's
              look and pace, its town and duels drawn on the Next's hardware
              sprite layer, with Sinclair's whole 48K ROM so it runs on
              NextZXOS 26.11. The original 48K game with its beeper sound;
              fits a 1MB Next. Enhanced colours are coming in a later version.
              Known issues: none found in testing; in JNext it runs 0.3 to 1.2
              percent faster than the original in every scene measured.
              Missing: not reached in testing: natural play to the end,
              joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite ammo
   3  Infinite money
   4  Bandit cannot move
   5  Bandit cannot shoot
   6  No horses
   7  No jumping boys
   8  No townsfolk

  The archive's POKEs checked against this exact 48K release, written where
  the game's loader copies its code from; Infinite ammo and Infinite money
  corrected so the original display and arithmetic still work.

